<!--
  PATH FORM CORRECTED AGAIN (2026-09-10, second pass).

  MGL path rules, from MiSTer's own docs (mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/mgl):
    <rbf>       "Relative path to the core's RBF file from the SD root, excluding
                 its file extension" -- so it resolves under /media/fat ONLY. A core
                 sitting on a USB drive CANNOT be referenced by an MGL.
    <file path> "Path to game file relative to the core's games folder" -- documented
                 examples are bare (dummy.chd, cds/dummy.iso). With <setname>System573
                 the games folder is games/System573, searched ACROSS storages, so a
                 bare filename works on SD and USB alike. That is why this form is
                 preferable to the absolute /media/fat/... paths this file first used.

  History, so nobody repeats it: the original absolute /media/fat paths silently loaded
  NOTHING when the games live on USB (the core then autoloaded games/PSX/boot.rom -- the
  consumer Sony BIOS -- and showed the PlayStation logo). The first correction made them
  games/System573/<file>, which is wrong too: relative to the games folder that means
  games/System573/games/System573/<file>. Bare filenames are the documented form.

  Entries with paths OUTSIDE the games folder (the saves/ slot below, where present) are
  left as-is and are NOT verified against the docs.
-->
<!--
  *** RUN LAUNCHER (installed game) *** To install from CD the FIRST time, use
  hypbbc2p_install.mgl instead.

  WHY THE TWO BLANK IMAGES ARE GONE (2026-09-11, the restore fix):
  Main mounts every SC<n> CONF_STR slot inside parse_config() at CORE INIT --
  user_io_init() calls it BEFORE mgl_parse(). So slot 4 (the 16 MB flash save) is
  mounted at t~0 and the restore starts immediately. An index-2 blank flash from the
  .mgl then lands ON TOP of the restored image (ch3_dl outranks the saver's ch3
  drain) and flash_load_taken is already latched, so the load never re-arms ->
  blank flash -> "DO YOU WANT TO INITIALIZE FLASH-ROM?". Upstream A/B'd this on
  de10 2026-07-31 for ddrsbm and fixed ddrsbm_console.mgl, but never carried the fix
  to this file. Measured here 2026-09-11: a reinstall prompt on the second launch.
  The index-3 blank NVRAM is dropped for the same class of reason -- a CD-install
  game keeps its installed flag in the M48T58, so reloading a blank one every launch
  discards it.

  TEST C: hypbbc2p (Hyper Bishi Bashi Champ 2P) -- a CD-INSTALLER game. Launches the
  573 as a standalone console core (is_arcade_type=0) with a BLANK 16MB flash + BLANK
  8KB NVRAM and the CD mounted into the S1 (CUECHD) slot. On first boot, with the boot
  device set to CD-ROM, the BIOS runs the CD installer which re-programs the (now
  WRITABLE) onboard flash from the disc and writes an "installed" signature to NVRAM.

  SECURITY CASSETTE -- REQUIRES THE REAL gx908ja.u1 DUMP (corrected 2026-06-12):
  This .mgl loads games/System573/hypbbc2p.u1 on ioctl index 4 (= seceep per emu.sv:693;
  a 132-B image latches as X76F100 per the >=560 ZS01 / >=256 F041 / else F100 size
  tiers). That file MUST be the AUTHENTIC gx908ja.u1 dump, staged as hypbbc2p.u1 -- treat
  it like a BIOS, a required user-supplied artifact. (The MAME-"BAD_DUMP" gx908ja.u1,
  crc 8900eaff, is functionally complete and works -- HW-confirmed: boots+runs.)

  Why the SYNTH .u1 is NOT enough: there are TWO cassette checks.
    * BIOS BOOT signature check (runs FIRST, before the CD program loads): the BIOS
      reads cassette blocks 0,0,1,2 and verifies an authentic signature in block 1
      (data[8:15] = 81 00 29 00 00 18 eb 52). That signature is authentic-dump data,
      NOT derivable from game plaintext. A synthesized .u1 (tools/gen_seccart_u1.py)
      FAILS this and stalls at the on-screen "-11N" wall -- the CD program never loads.
    * In-game X76F100 check (game fn 0x80036ec4, disassembled in workflow w135q1s92,
      runs AFTER the CD program loads): plaintext read password e9 34 df 40 7a d1 a7 ff,
      then data[0:2]=="JA" + data[4]==~(d0+d1)&0xff. THIS is what gen_seccart_u1.py
      satisfies -- but with the synth .u1 the boot never reaches it.
  So: gen_seccart_u1.py is useful only for analyzing/unit-testing the in-game check;
  the real gx908ja.u1 is required to actually boot.

  TEST PROCEDURE (de-confounded: warm-reboot the MiSTer, /proc/uptime < 60s, then ONE
  load via this .mgl):
    1. Launch this .mgl.  2. In the OSD set "573 Boot Device" -> CD-ROM (status O[93]).
    3. Let the installer run (it can be lengthy -- the install copies CD -> flash). It
       ENDS at an on-screen prompt: ROM flash complete, press TEST to continue.
    4. AT THAT PROMPT: open the OSD, set "573 Boot Device" -> Flash ROM, exit the OSD,
       then press TEST. The game verifies the flash and loads. No reload or reboot is
       needed -- the DIP SW4 change is picked up live, mirroring the real cabinet.
       (Corrected 2026-09-11 from "set Flash ROM and reload", which is not what the
       game asks for; verified on hardware.)
  STATUS (2026-06-12): with the real gx908ja.u1 staged as hypbbc2p.u1 this path now WORKS
  on real hardware (de10) -- it clears the -11N security wall, the CD/ATAPI installer
  copies the disc to onboard flash (first HW run of the CD path; previously sim-only),
  the in-game ROM check is all-OK, and the attract/demo loop runs (boot-stage frame
  progression 1.9KB->29KB->38KB + an unambiguous game frame). Judge results with
  frame_diff, not vision.

  Requires: _Console/Konami_System_573.rbf + games/System573/{573bios.bin,
  flash16m_blank.bin, nvram8k_blank.bin, hypbbc2p.chd}.
-->
<mistergamedescription>
  <rbf>_Console/Konami_System_573</rbf>
  <!-- setname + absolute paths: see hyperbbc_console.mgl for the full rationale
       (PSX-name HomeDir misresolution + config/PSX.CFG status pollution). -->
  <setname>System573</setname>
  <!-- the .sav FIRST: docs/2026-09-29-sav-mount-order.md (a slot-4 mount after the downloads let the previous title's .sav seed this title's flash) -->
  <file delay="1" type="s" index="4" path="hypbbc2p.sav"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="0" path="573bios.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="4" path="hypbbc2p.u1"/>
  <file delay="2" type="s" index="1" path="hypbbc2p.chd"/>
  <!-- FLASH PERSISTENCE (slot 4): mount the 16 MB save so a CD install survives a
       reboot. The file MUST exist before launch -- Main does NOT auto-create it on this path (pre=0), it ejects the slot; create it first
       it (pre=1/type=2) on the first write-back, so the blank flash stands until
       the installer programs it, then the save is created. On later launches the
       saver LOADs it over the .mgl blank (held under CPU reset, plan D).
       *** PARENT VERIFY ON HW (gate-0 RISK R4): confirm a .mgl type="s" entry can
       point at a NOT-YET-EXISTENT saves/ path AND trigger Main's pre-allocate
       auto-create. If the .mgl schema rejects it, the fallback is one
       user_io_file_mount(savepath, 4, 1, 16*1024*1024) in the PSX support file's
       load callback. Path = saves/System573/<basename>.sav per FileGenerateSavePath. -->
  <!-- SAVE PATH, CORRECTED 2026-09-11 (measured, not inferred).
       This entry used to read path="saves/System573/<name>.sav". A .mgl type="s"
       path is resolved games-folder-relative and taken VERBATIM -- it is NOT run
       through Main's FileGenerateSavePath. Proof: after a successful hypbbc2p CD
       install, config/System573.s4 held
         ../usb0/games/System573/saves/System573/hypbbc2p.sav
       i.e. games/System573/ + the literal path above. That directory does not
       exist, so Main EJECTS a slot whose file is missing (pre=0; there is no auto-create on this path) -- see
       file: the core programmed its 16 MB flash and the save went nowhere, and the
       next launch offered to initialize the flash again.
       A bare filename lands it in games/System573/, which exists. -->
  <reset delay="1"/>
</mistergamedescription>
